{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/657861-killer-instinct-merit","id":657861,"title":"Killer Instinct Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T07:36:49-07:00","id":657861,"title":"Killer Instinct Merit","content":"So, the basic variant of this merit allows for the user to convert a single point of inflicted bashing to lethal. This, from what I understand, is that the user knows where/how to hit the body to cause serious damage with just his fist. A mortal can take this so there is nothing supernatural at play, just Dexter-esque knowledge. The advanced version, however, is beast only. So, with this version, the beast can destroy armor and can inflict agg damage. So my question is, how does the beast achieve this? Is the horror channeling supernatural energy or whatever in order to inflict that kind of damage?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, if you have the advanced version, you can use all the benefits of the basic merit without taking a turn to observe. Does this mean that if the beast punches his opponent, he converts one bashing to lethal, and then (provided he took a turn to observe) can turn that lethal into a single agg point of damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7474,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","user":"Tylerjohnny1","date":". 09-09-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:59:59-07:00","id":658152,"title":"","content":"Well when you inflict aggravated it had to already be lethal. Meaning if the first is just knowing exactly how hard and where you need to punch someone to break a bone the second is knowing how to convert a blow that would break the bones into one that shatters the bone and tears the muscles. The armor destroying property is basically being able to apply the increased damage principle of converting bashing into knowing the weak points in the armor and hitting those.<br /> <br /> I spoke with a friend of mine and he figures if you operate on the idea that the base form requires no action to identify the maim points then yeah you could theoretically upgrade a one bashing punch straight to a one aggravated damage punch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 09-09-2015, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:55:09-07:00","id":658618,"title":"","content":"Of course doing that requires a turn of observation, and only grants at most 3 agg every 2 turns. Really best used as a finisher against an opponent that can't readily heal agg, or to soften a target up for the troupe's hitters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}